### The CLI option shape adaptation

The upstream CLI returned separate `owner` and `rationale` fields. The committed
Red test asserts one shape:

```text
expect(options).toMatchObject({ newDebtMetadata: { owner, rationale } });
```

Upstream's shape fails that assertion. The ported options carry
`newDebtMetadata: NewDebtReviewMetadata` instead. The `--owner` and
`--rationale` arguments, their pairing rule, and the forwarded value are
unchanged.

### The dependency arity test update

The upstream commits changed the `apply` and `preview` dependency signatures to
take a third argument. Upstream updated two assertions in
`packages/architecture-enforcement/src/__tests__/architecture-reconciliation-cli.test.ts`.
That port carries the same two assertions. A probe showed that Vitest
`toHaveBeenCalledWith` does not match a trailing `undefined` argument, so the
two assertions had to follow the signature.

